# Python only

- Use Python for all application, script, and tooling code.
- Do not add other languages (JavaScript/TypeScript, Go, Java, etc.) or their package ecosystems unless the user explicitly asks.
- Prefer the standard library; add third-party Python packages only when needed.
- Use `.py` modules. Add `requirements.txt` or `pyproject.toml` when dependencies appear.
- Config and docs are fine (`.gitignore`, `README.md`, YAML/TOML, etc.).
